# Recreate this Three.js scene: Particle Sphere

You are an expert Three.js creative developer. Produce a **single self-contained `index.html`**
that renders the scene below **exactly** as specified — same geometry, shaders, colors, motion,
and postprocessing. Load Three.js **r0.143.0** via an ES-module importmap from unpkg; no build
step, no bundler, pure ES modules in one `<script type="module">`. Hardcode every value given
here as fixed constants.

## What it looks like
A dense sphere of glowing points displaced along its normal by two octaves of Simplex noise,
shaded with a deep-blue-to-magenta vertical gradient and a Fresnel rim. It sits on a dark indigo
field laced with soft blue-and-pink corner flames and drifting ambient motes. As the page scrolls
the camera dives toward the churning core, the surface noise swells, the spin accelerates, and the
filled orb dissolves open at its centre into a glowing shell; the cursor parallaxes the view and
parts the points around the pointer.

